	<!-- Programmatic SEO Below-the-fold Content -->
	<div slot="seo-content" class="prose prose-invert max-w-none flex flex-col gap-8 text-vercel-light-gray">
		<section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">How to Calculate Semester GPA Manually</h2>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
				To calculate your credit-weighted Semester Grade Point Average (GPA), you must multiply the point value of the letter grade received in each course by the credit hours assigned to that course. After summing these grade points, divide the grand total by the sum of all credit hours attempted.
			</p>
			
			<div class="bg-black/50 border border-vercel-border p-5 rounded font-mono text-xs flex flex-col gap-3 my-2 text-center text-white overflow-x-auto scrollbar-none">
				<div class="text-white font-bold border-b border-vercel-border pb-2 mb-2">
					THE WEIGHTED GPA FORMULA
				</div>
				{"$$GPA = \\frac{\\sum (Grade\\,Value \\times Credit\\,Hours)}{\\sum Credit\\,Hours}$$"}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Step-by-Step Calculation Example</h3>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
				Suppose you took the following four courses during your semester:
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm pl-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">
				<li><strong>English:</strong> Grade A (4.0 points) &times; 3 credits = 12.0 grade points</li>
				<li><strong>Calculus I:</strong> Grade B+ (3.3 points) &times; 4 credits = 13.2 grade points</li>
				<li><strong>General Chemistry:</strong> Grade A- (3.7 points) &times; 4 credits = 14.8 grade points</li>
				<li><strong>Intro to History:</strong> Grade B (3.0 points) &times; 3 credits = 9.0 grade points</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
				To compute the overall term GPA:
			</p>
			<ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-sm pl-2 flex flex-col gap-2">
				<li>
					Sum the grade points: <code class="font-mono text-xs text-white bg-vercel-card px-1 py-0.5 rounded border border-vercel-border">12.0 + 13.2 + 14.8 + 9.0 = 49.0</code>.
				</li>
				<li>
					Sum the credit hours: <code class="font-mono text-xs text-white bg-vercel-card px-1 py-0.5 rounded border border-vercel-border">3 + 4 + 4 + 3 = 14</code>.
				</li>
				<li>
					Divide total grade points by total credits: <code class="font-mono text-xs text-white bg-vercel-card px-1 py-0.5 rounded border border-vercel-border">49.0 / 14 = 3.50</code>.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
				Your final credit-weighted Semester Grade Point Average is <strong>3.50</strong>, qualifying for honors recognition.
			</p>
		</section>

		<!-- Crawlable FAQ Schema -->
		<section class="border-t border-vercel-border/50 pt-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
			<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h3>
			
			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
