					<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">What is a credit hour?</h4>
					<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
						A credit hour represents the academic weight or workload of a course. A standard lecture class is normally worth 3 credits, while labs and intensive math/science classes usually carry 4 credits.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
					<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">How does a failing grade impact my GPA?</h4>
					<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
						An "F" grade contributes 0.0 grade points, but the credit hours are still factored into the denominator. This significantly pulls down your total average.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
					<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Are pass/fail courses calculated in my GPA?</h4>
					<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
						No. Pass/fail classes do not carry point equivalents on a 4.0 scale. They are excluded from GPA averages.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
					<h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Is my data secure?</h4>
					<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
						Yes. Calculations are computed 100% locally in your web browser. No course details, credits, or grade histories are sent to external databases.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
